      "stdout": "Download an asset file by type and resource ID.\r\n\r\nAGENT QUICKSTART (driving this as an agent? start here):\r\n  Browse commands:  lyra-cli <domain> --help\r\n\r\nUSAGE:\r\n  lyra-cli <domain> <[subdomain] ...> <action> [--flags] [--options]\r\n\r\n\r\nOPTIONS:\r\n  -h, --help                            Print this help message and exit\r\n      --type TEXT REQUIRED              Material asset type key. Use `music` for music; use supported\r\n                                        visual/audio asset keys such as `sticker`, `effect`,\r\n                                        `transition`, `text_template`, or `sound` for other materials.\r\n      --resource-id TEXT REQUIRED       Material resource ID returned by `material search`, `material\r\n                                        topic`, or `material query`.\r\n      --resource-platform <vimo|heycan|loki|music> \r\n                                        Material source. Use `vimo`, `heycan`, or `loki` for visual/audio\r\n                                        assets; use `music` for music. Numeric values `1`, `2`, `3` are\r\n                                        kept for compatibility.\r\n      --resource-dir TEXT               Target directory for the downloaded asset. Uses the platform\r\n                                        default material cache when omitted.\r\n      --channel <online|test|local_test> \r\n                                        Material request channel. Use `test` or `local_test` for internal\r\n                                        test resources.\r\n  -v, --version                         Show version information and exit.\r\n      --jq TEXT                         Pretty-print JSON output; with an optional selector like\r\n                                        .result.items[0].id, output the selected JSON value instead of\r\n                                        the full schema envelope.\r\n\r\nWHEN TO USE\r\n  - A downstream workflow needs a local file instead of a platform resource ID.\r\n  - Music downloads save the preview audio; visual/audio assets use their material package or file.\r\n\r\nINPUT\r\n  Use resource_id from material search, material topic, or material query.\r\n\r\nEXAMPLES\r\n  $ lyra-cli material download --type sticker --resource-id \"7586591573920664856\"\r\n  $ lyra-cli material download --type music --resource-id \"6944678306690085633\" --resource-platform music\r\n  $ lyra-cli material download --type transition --resource-id \"7602154462643375402\" --resource-dir /tmp/materials\r\n\r\nOUTPUT\r\n  Returns result.path with the downloaded local path.\r\n",
